Acknowledgements
================

Shuo is an application that calls locally-downloaded speech models. Model
weights are the property of their respective authors and are NOT redistributed
by this repository (they are fetched from GitHub Releases / Hugging Face at
install time by the user).

Primary ASR model (fine-tuned package, prompt-controlled output style):

- Base model: Qwen3-ASR-1.7B by Qwen Team — Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B
  Official repo: https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-ASR
  Technical report: https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.21337
- GGUF conversion tooling: ggml-org/llama.cpp — MIT License
  Official GGUF release: https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B-GGUF
- The distributed fine-tuned package is a LoRA fine-tune of the base model
  (transcription with prompt-controlled output style, in one pass); provenance
  (base / adapter / prompts / timestamp) is recorded in the package's
  shuo-model.json marker file.

Fallback ASR model (ONNX backend, optional):

- Pre-built ONNX package: Daumee/Qwen3-ASR-0.6B-ONNX-CPU
  https://huggingface.co/Daumee/Qwen3-ASR-0.6B-ONNX-CPU
- ONNX export lineage: andrewleech/qwen3-asr-onnx
  https://github.com/andrewleech/qwen3-asr-onnx

Denoiser (bundled with the app):

- src-tauri/resources/denoise.onnx — streaming NFT_960 denoiser (48 kHz).

Runtime libraries: llama.cpp (MIT), ONNX Runtime (MIT), Tauri (MIT/Apache-2.0),
cpal (Apache-2.0/MIT), tokenizers (Apache-2.0), ureq (MIT/Apache-2.0).
